---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { archiveStatus } from '../../data/content';
import metadata from '../../../public/data/city-metadata.json';
import skyMetadata from '../../../public/data/sky-metadata.json';
---
<Layout title="Data, sources & credits — Cville AI Explorers" description="Open geographic data, attribution, archive coverage, and the visualization choices behind our cosmic Charlottesville explorer.">
  <main id="main" class="content-main"><span class="eyebrow">A REAL CITY. AN OPEN FOUNDATION.</span><h1>Behind the<br /><em>constellation.</em></h1><p class="lead">The city is built from public Charlottesville geographic data. The portal rooms and landmark model are creative interpretations.</p>
    <div class="stats-grid"><div class="stat"><strong>{metadata.polygons.toLocaleString()}</strong><span>Imported building polygons</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>{(metadata.sourcedHeights / metadata.buildings * 100).toFixed(1)}%</strong><span>Building records with usable sourced heights</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>{metadata.roadSegments.toLocaleString()}</strong><span>Road centerline segments</span></div></div>
    <h2>Geographic sources</h2><ul><li><a href="https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=431d3b5cde454e9f9c65725cc2f44c97">Existing Structure Area</a> — City of Charlottesville building footprints and HeightFt attributes.</li><li><a href="https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=5ea50546852444a890dc55c9d68104f8">Road Centerlines</a> — City of Charlottesville street geometry.</li></ul><p>Both datasets are published under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International</a>. Attribution: City of Charlottesville, via the <a href="https://opendata.charlottesville.org/">City Open Data Portal</a>. We have clipped the data, projected it to a local meter-based scene, rounded coordinates, converted heights from feet to meters, and applied visualization styling.</p>
    <h2>Snapshot & visualization choices</h2><p>Retrieved {new Date(metadata.retrievedAt).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' })}. The snapshot covers a bounded city area, not every building in Charlottesville or Albemarle County.</p><ul><li>{metadata.estimatedHeights} building records without usable heights use a 7-meter fallback, marked as estimated in the data.</li><li>The first prototype uses a flat ground plane; surveyed terrain is a later stage.</li><li>Most venue coordinates are approximate and need address-level verification. UVA School of Data Science’s building-center pin is from <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/1291005629">OpenStreetMap way 1291005629</a> (© <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap contributors</a>, ODbL), with its address confirmed by UVA’s event page.</li><li>The Data Science building model is a stylized original illustration. UVA-area footprint completeness is not yet audited.</li><li>Road widths are illustrative, not sourced measurements.</li><li>Flight has ground clearance and a region boundary; full building collisions are a future interaction refinement.</li><li>The Studio IX and Data Science rooms are artistic community exhibits, not reproductions of real interiors.</li></ul>
    <details class="background-credits"><summary>Background data credits</summary><p>{skyMetadata.stars.toLocaleString()} stars from {skyMetadata.starsCredit} {skyMetadata.constellations} constellation outlines from {skyMetadata.constellationsCredit}</p><p>The <a href={skyMetadata.source}>pinned d3-celestial data snapshot</a> is credited with its <a href="/data/sky-LICENSE.txt">BSD-3-Clause license notice</a>. Catalog positions are J2000.0; we apply precession and local sidereal rotation for Charlottesville using the device’s current UTC clock. Stars below the mathematical horizon are hidden. While the map camera looks down, the celestial backdrop uses an elevated gaze along the same bearing; looking up in free flight uses that gaze. Cosmic night styling remains visible at all hours. Refraction, nutation, aberration, proper motion, planets, and daylight simulation are not included.</p><p><a href="/data/sky-metadata.json">Snapshot metadata</a> · <a href="/data/sky.json">Catalog and outlines</a></p></details>
    <h2>Community & event sources</h2><p>Community content comes from <a href="https://www.cvaiex.org/">cvaiex.org</a>. Event content is sourced from public <a href="https://www.meetup.com/cville-tech/">Charlottesville Technologists</a> listings, with a source link on each imported event.</p><div class="source-note">{archiveStatus}<br />The group page reported 175 past events during research. The full archive redirected to login, and the preview contained an anomalous date. We are not treating that preview as a verified complete archive.</div>
    <h2>Venue walking & Downtown Mall sources</h2><p>Studio IX, UVA Data Science, and Kardinal Hall have artistic indoor walking scenes with local boundary and furniture collisions. They are not measured real-world interiors.</p><p>The outdoor walk uses a curated <a href="/data/storefronts.json">JSON storefront catalog</a>. Names, addresses, and descriptions are source-linked to business-owned websites; individual records carry their checked date. Physical slots and façade shapes are illustrative. The first seven stops do not represent a complete business inventory, and listing data does not imply live opening hours.</p><p>Four dated photographs are distributed locally under their individual CC BY 3.0, CC BY-SA 4.0, or CC0 terms. <a href="/mall/">The mall directory lists each creator, original image, date, license, and resizing/cropping credit</a>. Shared-alike photo derivatives retain their source license.</p>
    <h2>Machine-readable exports</h2><ul><li><a href="/data/content.json">Community, places, and events JSON</a></li><li><a href="/content.md">Readable content Markdown</a></li><li><a href="/data/city-metadata.json">City snapshot metadata</a></li><li><a href="/data/city.json">Projected building and road snapshot JSON</a></li><li><a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a> · <a href="/robots.txt">robots.txt</a> · <a href="/sitemap-index.xml">Sitemap</a></li></ul>
    <h2>What’s next</h2><p>Validate destination pins and the city boundary, add audited historical venues, bring in terrain, and refine the flight and room experience. Monticello, Albemarle County, and mountain destinations are future region packs.</p>
  </main>
</Layout>
